    {
      "bbox": [
        388,
        1241,
        1949,
        2014
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Because an ample supply of blood for transfusions and other medical purposes will be an important factor in civilian defense and because we can anticipate a call for blood for the armed services, I have named Dr. Samuel Frant, First Deputy Commissioner of the Department of Health, chairman of a municipal employees committee and instructed him to begin enrolling blood donors immediately among City employees. Dr. Frant will work with the Red Cross Blood Program which will handle the actual collection of blood from donors and process it.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.1369,
          "min": -0.625
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": 0.0,
          "min": 0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 99,
          "mean": 0.0,
          "min": 0.0
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 57963,
        "area_px": 1213610,
        "density": 0.04776,
        "chars": 540,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 9.32
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        388,
        2053,
        1961,
        2842
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "You may know that for two years the Blood Program has been collecting blood and has been supplying a substantial amount of blood to our municipal and voluntary hospitals to meet the blood needs of our civilian ill and injured. Some City departments have been participants in the program and have received blood through it for their sick and injured workers. This phase of the program will continue and Dr. Frant will explain how the blood donors in your department may be assured of an adequate supply when they or members of their families are in need of blood.",
